== Failure found in this round and fixed
The Yosys stat gate. Rounds 1-2 compared counts of `synth -flatten` on the sv2v text and reported them as not
an identity test (Yosys 0.33 counts move when unrelated text is read). This round adds a canonical form:
scripts/netlist_canon.py relabels the elaborated netlist (proc; flatten; opt_clean -purge; memory_collect) by
colour refinement from cell types, parameters and port names, and writes it without names in label order. Two
netlists give the same file when they are the same graph up to names; then the same synth gives the same stat.
At 5c61580 the canonical netlists differed from main's in all four configs (sigil_core and sigil_soc_top,
default and SRAM_OREG). `netlist_canon.py diff` on the round-1 labels: 6 cells per side, all at vls_done /
vls_fault. Main clears the VLS sequencer on ((!vls_is || vls_done) || vls_fault) || trap_fire; the branch's
off path computed vls_end = vls_done || vls_fault and cleared on (!vls_is || vls_end) || trap_fire. Same
function (the equivalence proofs pass), other structure: after opt, opt_merge shares the branch's
vls_done || vls_fault with two existing terms (vec_dirty_i, vstart_we_i), one $logic_or fewer (846 vs 847).
Fix 871b2dd: the generate-if selects the whole clear condition, off = main's expression as written, on =
unchanged. Afterwards every canonical netlist is identical to main's (below). The FPGA setting is unchanged:
the canonical sigil_soc_top netlist with SIGIL_FPGA_TIMING + SIGIL_VRF_OREG is the same file at 5c61580 and
871b2dd (sha256 2ffc6d6aba25a55a), and F0 gives the same numbers.
Runs at 5c61580 before the fix (01:29-03:45Z, same method), all passing, superseded by the reruns: lint 5.048 /
5.020 31 runs 0 warnings, make test, core-test (off 4555 s, on 7335 s), socrtl, riscv-tests 123/123 in both
settings; riscv-dv on the adf4c97 flow 100/100 main and branch; F0 WNS +0.690 ns; the equivalence proofs.
core-test at 871b2dd is line-identical, cycles included, to 5c61580 in both settings (412 lines).

